  "text": "הוצאת:\n\nricao: We mean $51,\\dots, 254$ without commas. sách revo: Tiết 2 yên, phát tính hết đứt 254, dùng dấu cách. The polynomial given is \\( Q(z) = z^3 + sz + t \\), where \\( x, y, z \\) are its roots. By Vieta's formulas, we know:\n1. \\( x + y + z = 0 \\) (since there is no linear term)\n2. \\( x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 0 \\) (since there is no quadratic term)\n3. \\( xy + yz + zx = s \\)\n4. \\( xyz = -t \\)\n\nIt is given that \\( |x|^2 + |y|^2 + |z|^2 = 352 \\). Since \\( |x|^2 + |y|^2 + |z|^2 = x \\bar{x} + y \\bar{y} + z \\bar{z} = (x + y + z) |x|^2 + (xy + yz + zx) \\), and considering \\( x + y + z = 0 \\) and \\( x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 0 \\), this implies \\( xy + yz + zx = s = 352 \\).\n\nTo find \\( b^2 \\), where \\( b \\) is the base of the isosceles triangle, we use the fact that the feet of the perpendiculars from \\( O \\) (the origin in the complex plane) to the sides of the triangle are the midpoints of those sides. This implies the distances to be related as follows: \\( b^2 + c^2 = 352 \\) (where \\( c \\) is the height of the triangle).\n\nThe distance from \\( x \\) to \\( y \\) (base) is \\( |x - y| = \\sqrt{(x^2 + y^2 - 352}) = \\sqrt{(s - 512)} \\): similarly, the distance from \\( y \\) to \\( z \\) and \\( z \\) to \\( x \\) are the same, i.e., \\( \\sqrt{(s - 512)} \\).\n\nTherefore, \\( b = 2 \\cdot \\sqrt{(s - 512)} \\), and \\( b^2 = 4 (s - 512) = 4(352) = 1408 \\) when \\( s = 352 \\).\n\nTherefore, the answer is:\n\n\\boxed{1408}",
